journal\2026-11-11-session.md:23:- **One compartment fails the 24 h check, as predicted**: 7.6-fold fall from peak to 24 h vs. the label's 37-fold. With the label's 4 L/kg volume it also underpredicts the peak ~5-fold (851 vs. 4,817 pg/mL).
journal\2026-11-11-session.md:26:- **Label clearance/volume don't match its own concentrations**: fit implies ~230 L/day and ~1 L/kg vs. label's ~600 L/day and ~4 L/kg (probably different studies). An AUC check gives ~240 L/day too.
journal\2026-11-11-session.md:36:- **Alesse Table I has SHBG and CL/F on days 1, 6, 21** (SHBG 57 → 81 → 93 nmol/L; CL/F 53.7 → 40.8 → 28.4 mL/h/kg). Use these to calibrate the SHBG effect instead of tuning by eye.
journal\2026-11-11-session.md:43:- `src/minipill/params.py` — norethindrone parameters with sources; `BODY_WEIGHT_KG = 60` is my assumption.
journal\2026-11-12-session.md:19:- **Half-life from Table I**: ln 2 · (Vz/F) / (CL/F) = 34.3 h. Body weight cancels, so no weight assumption.
journal\2026-11-12-session.md:30:- **The gap SHBG has to explain**: without SHBG the model's day-21 AUC is 35 ng·h/mL vs. 68 measured, and the low before the next pill is 0.84 vs. 1.9 ng/mL. The AUC gap (×1.9) matches the label's CL/F fall from day 1 to day 21 (53.7 → 28.4 mL/h/kg, ×1.9).
journal\2026-11-12-session.md:32:- The label's day-1 AUC and CL/F imply a body weight of ~53 kg, not my assumed 60 kg. Doesn't matter for levonorgestrel since everything is in L/h directly.
journal\2026-11-12-session.md:57:1. Add SHBG, calibrated to Alesse Table I (days 1, 6, 21: SHBG 57 → 81 → 93 nmol/L; CL/F 53.7 → 40.8 → 28.4 mL/h/kg). Target: day-21 AUC 68 and low ~1.9 ng/mL.
journal\2026-11-12-session.md:89:- **Week-3 peak is low**: 4.94 vs. 6.0 ± 2.65 ng/mL. Likely because the label's Vz/F shrinks (2.66 → 1.43 L/kg) and the model keeps volume fixed.
journal\2026-11-12-session.md:90:- **Not only binding**: the label's unbound levonorgestrel also rose (+83%) and unbound clearance fell (2.79 → 1.57 L/h/kg); free fraction barely changed (1.92 → 1.78%). So in the model SHBG stands for the whole estrogen effect on clearance.
