74	213:     </div>
75	214:     <p>How the model does it: while active pills are taken, SHBG rises toward a plateau (half-way in about 3 days) and falls back in the placebo week. Levonorgestrel's clearance is scaled by (57 ÷ SHBG)<sup>1.33</sup>. The SHBG curve is fitted to the three measured values, and the strength (1.33) to the measured day-6 and day-21 exposure. The model then gives a low point of 2.0 ng/mL before the n
76	215:     <p class="callout">Caveat: the label shows that the unbound (free) levonorgestrel also rose and its unbound clearance fell, so the estrogen effect isn't only binding. In the model, SHBG stands for the whole effect. The model's week-3 peak is also low (4.9 vs. 6.0 ± 2.7 ng/mL), likely because the drug's volume of distribution also shrinks, which isn't modeled.</p>
