195:   <section aria-labelledby="h-shbg">
196:     <div class="section-head">
197:       <h2 id="h-shbg">SHBG: why the combined pill builds up</h2>
198:       <p class="say"><span class="tag">In plain words</span>The combined pill has two hormones, and one helps the other stick around. Its estrogen tells the liver to make more of a carrier protein, SHBG. Levonorgestrel rides on SHBG in the blood, and while it's held there the liver clears it more slowly. The minipill has no estrogen, so this never happens.</p>
199:     </div>
200:     <div class="chain" aria-label="Cause and effect chain">Estrogen (ethinyl estradiol) → liver makes more <b>SHBG</b> → more levonorgestrel held in the blood → cleared more slowly → levels build up over the pack</div>
201:     <div class="explain">
202:       <div class="step"><h3>What SHBG is</h3><p>Sex hormone–binding globulin: a protein made by the liver that carries sex hormones in the blood. Levonorgestrel binds it strongly; about half of the levonorgestrel in blood is on SHBG.</p></div>
203:       <div class="step"><h3>What the estrogen does</h3><p>In the Alesse study, SHBG rose from 57 to 81 to 93 nmol/L on days 1, 6 and 21, about 60% higher by week 3. It levels off within about two weeks and drifts back down in the placebo week.</p></div>
204:       <div class="step"><h3>What that does to levonorgestrel</h3><p>Over the same days, levonorgestrel's clearance fell almost by half (53.7 → 28.4 mL/h/kg), so levels on day 21 were about twice day 1's. That stored-up hormone is what carries the combined pill through a missed pill.</p></div>
205:     </div>
206:     <div class="panel">
207:       <div class="legend">
208:         <span><svg width="22" height="10" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="1" y1="5" x2="21" y2="5" stroke="var(--combo)" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>SHBG in the model</span>
209:         <span><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="7" y1="1" x2="7" y2="13" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.5"/><circle cx="7" cy="7" r="4" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--combo)" stroke-width="2"/></svg>Alesse measured (mean ± SD)</span>
210:         <span><svg width="22" height="10" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="1" y1="5" x2="21" y2="5" stroke="var(--mini)" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>Minipill: no estrogen, SHBG stays at baseline</span>
211:       </div>
212:       <div class="chart" id="chart-shbg"></div>
213:     </div>
214:     <p>How the model does it: while active pills are taken, SHBG rises toward a plateau (half-way in about 3 days) and falls back in the placebo week. Levonorgestrel's clearance is scaled by (57 ÷ SHBG)<sup>1.33</sup>. The SHBG curve is fitted to the three measured values, and the strength (1.33) to the measured day-6 and day-21 exposure. The model then gives a low point of 2.0 ng/mL before the n
215:     <p class="callout">Caveat: the label shows that the unbound (free) levonorgestrel also rose and its unbound clearance fell, so the estrogen effect isn't only binding. In the model, SHBG stands for the whole effect. The model's week-3 peak is also low (4.9 vs. 6.0 ± 2.7 ng/mL), likely because the drug's volume of distribution also shrinks, which isn't modeled.</p>
216:   </section>
217: 
218:   <section aria-labelledby="h-month">
219:     <div class="section-head">
220:       <h2 id="h-month">A month of pills</h2>
221:       <p class="say"><span class="tag">In plain words</span>The minipill is taken every day with no break and its level looks the same each day. The combined pill's level climbs for three weeks, then drains during the placebo week.</p>
222:       <p>The minipill: one pill daily for 28 days. The combined pill: 21 active pills, then 7 placebo. Open points are what Alesse measured on days 1, 6 and 21. The faint dashed line is the combined pill without SHBG, which falls well short by day 21.</p>
223:     </div>
224:     <div class="panel">
225:       <div class="legend">
226:         <span><svg width="22" height="10" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="1" y1="5" x2="21" y2="5" stroke="var(--mini)" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>Norethindrone</span>
227:         <span><svg width="22" height="10" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="1" y1="5" x2="21" y2="5" stroke="var(--combo)" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>Levonorgestrel, with SHBG</span>
228:         <span><svg width="22" height="10" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="1" y1="5" x2="21" y2="5" stroke="var(--combo)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="6 5" opacity="0.5"/></svg>Without SHBG</span>
229:         <span><svg width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="7" y1="1" x2="7" y2="13" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.5"/><circle cx="7" cy="7" r="4" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--combo)" stroke-width="2"/></svg>Alesse measured</span>
