236:   <section aria-labelledby="h-late">
237:     <div class="section-head">
238:       <h2 id="h-late">When a pill is late</h2>
239:       <p class="say"><span class="tag">In plain words</span>Make the day-15 pill late for both and compare. Each line is shown as a share of that pill's own normal daily low (100%), so the two can be read on one scale.</p>
240:       <p>Pills on time until day 15; that pill is taken late (later pills stay on their usual time), skipped, or two pills are missed (the missed pill and the next one then taken together at +48 h, as CDC advises). CDC treats a minipill more than 3 h late as missed, but a combined pill needs no backup until 48 h.</p>
241:     </div>
242:     <div class="panel">
243:       <div class="controls">
244:         <div class="slider-row">
245:           <label for="late">Day-15 pill taken</label>
246:           <input type="range" id="late" min="0" max="23" step="0.5" value="3" aria-describedby="late-val">
247:           <span class="late-val" id="late-val">3 h late</span>
