251:           <button type="button" data-late="3">3 h late</button>
252:           <button type="button" data-late="12">12 h late</button>
253:           <button type="button" data-late="skip">1 pill missed</button>
254:           <button type="button" data-late="skip2">2 pills missed</button>
255:         </div>
256:       </div>
257:       <div class="legend">
258:         <span><svg width="22" height="10" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="1" y1="5" x2="21" y2="5" stroke="var(--mini)" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>Minipill</span>
259:         <span><svg width="22" height="10" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="1" y1="5" x2="21" y2="5" stroke="var(--combo)" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>Combined pill (with SHBG)</span>
260:         <span><svg width="22" height="10" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="1" y1="5" x2="21" y2="5" stroke="var(--ink-2)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="2 4"/></svg>Usual daily low = 100%</span>
261:       </div>
262:       <div class="chart" id="chart-late"></div>
263:     </div>
264:     <div class="versus">
265:       <div class="vcol">
266:         <h3><i class="dot" style="background:var(--mini)"></i>Minipill</h3>
267:         <div class="vrow"><span class="k">Lowest level</span><span class="n" id="m-min">–</span></div>
268:         <div class="vrow"><span class="k">Extra time below usual low</span><span class="n" id="m-time">–</span></div>
269:       </div>
270:       <div class="vcol">
271:         <h3><i class="dot" style="background:var(--combo)"></i>Combined pill</h3>
272:         <div class="vrow"><span class="k">Lowest level</span><span class="n" id="c-min">–</span></div>
273:         <div class="vrow"><span class="k">Extra time below usual low</span><span class="n" id="c-time">–</span></div>
274:       </div>
275:     </div>
276:     <p class="summary" id="summary"></p>
277:     <p class="callout">At each pill's CDC limit the dips are similar: the minipill 3 h late dips 23%; the combined pill with one pill missed (under 48 h) dips 28%. This compares hormone levels only. The minipill also works by thickening cervical mucus, which isn't modeled.</p>
278:   </section>
279: 
280:   <footer>
281:     <p>Models from src/minipill/params.py. Norethindrone: two compartments fitted to its label (F = 0.65). Levonorgestrel: two compartments fitted to Alesse day 1 (F = 1, absorption rate assumed 0.8 /h), with an SHBG effect fitted to Alesse days 6 and 21. Combined-pill curves with SHBG are simulated in Python (scripts/export_comparison_data.py) and stored in this page. One-compartment versions use
282:     <p>An educational model built for a course project, not medical advice. Hormone level stands in for protection here; the minipill also works by thickening cervical mucus, which the model doesn't simulate.</p>
283:   </footer>
